+/// Properties the recovery sets itself that the stock file may already carry.
+///
+/// The first three are the build's version and patch levels of its own
+/// ramdisk's system and vendor partition, which are older than those
+/// installed beside it whenever the phone has taken an update. The phone's
+/// secure services read these to tell the secure world which build is
+/// running, and keys the installed system made are refused when they say the
+/// wrong one, so they are left out here for the recovery to fill in from the
+/// installed system once it has that mounted.
+///
+/// The last three decide whether adbd keeps root and whether a computer is
+/// asked to authorize; the stock file carries the opposite values, and which
+/// of two lines init takes is not left to chance.
+const REPLACED: [&str; 6] = [
+    "ro.build.version.release",
+    "ro.build.version.security_patch",
+    "ro.vendor.build.security_patch",
+    "ro.secure",
+    "ro.adb.secure",
+    "ro.debuggable",
+];
 
